text:
Some things that do not;
Some things that do not reach
Some are far away.

That I did never know,
That I never knew;
I never knew that I was ever.

Some keep the Sabbath going to church;
Some keep the Sabbath going to church;
Some keep the Sabbath going to church.

So we will leave them in the night;
And when they are gone, we will not tell;
And when they are gone, we will not tell;

I went to heaven, and I went to heaven.

And when I went, I looked to heaven.

And I saw a light;

And I saw a man;

And I saw a bird.

And I saw a lion.

And I saw a man.

And I saw a child;

And I saw a serpent.

For an inch in the evening.

I had nothing to do;
I never expected it;
I thought I would go;
But a master of mine
Went to see me, and then said,
I am a little like him!

The devil shall not touch my eyes!

'T was just this time last year I died;
'T was just this time last year I died.

'T was just this time last year I died;
'T was just this time last year I died;
'T was just this time last year I died;
'T was just this time last year I died;
'T was just this time
